eme":"reach","type":"I"},{"cost":3600,"cost":{"$fix":15461882265600},"cost_reason":"docs/MVP/28 \u00A77: late Iron project (prerequisite depth \u003E= 3) costs 2x the derived cost so research slows toward the end of the age","effects":[{"kind":"rule","text":"one founding band may establish a colony up to 10 sea tiles from a known owned coast, only at unclaimed habitable land with a safe landing, ship, 2-season rations, and normal founding costs; no teleportation or extra population"}],"era":4,"flavor":"A new settlement is planned beyond the horizon.","id":"TER-09","idx":433,"lineage":"TER","moment":"A family boards a ship with seed and tools.","name":"Frontier Colonies","practice":[{"action":"scout","share":100}],"requires":["TER-08","SEA-06"],"status":"numeric","theme":"reach","type":"I"},{"cost":{"$fix":41231686041600},"effects":[{"kind":"mod","note":"30% off the Fief-mode farm-tile upkeep (base 10% of yield, P, user decision D4 of docs 27)","op":"mult","stat":"claim_upkeep_farm","value":{"$fix":3006477107}},{"kind":"rule","text":"The base upkeep is a Fief-chapter economy rule from KEY-5: held farm tiles pay 10% of their yield as grain to the non-farming staff of the nearest staffed seat, so no grain is created or lost; this project cuts it to 7%."}],"era":5,"flavor":"The estate holds the land so the lord need not.","id":"TER-10","idx":434,"lineage":"TER","moment":"A steward counts sheaves at a manor barn.","name":"Manorial Estates","practice":[{"action":"mark","share":100}],"requires":["TER-08","GOV-09"],"status":"numeric","theme":"reach","type":"I"},{"cost":{"$fix":77309411328000},"effects":[{"action":"colonize","kind":"unlock_action"},{"kind":"rule","text":"With SEA-12, a daughter band or a decree may found across the sea up to 40 tiles (the channel is 31 to 39), where outriggers reach 24 (P, docs/MVP/38 \u00A75.2)."},{"kind":"rule","text":"A colony is a settlement founded across an ocean; it pays a distance-based Overreach strain and carries a bounded, seeded 